    right_hip_1_joint: -0.3321831524372101
    right_hip_2_joint: -0.013716209679841995
    right_hip_3_joint: 0.08450339734554291
    right_knee_joint: -0.6432819366455078
    right_ankle_1_joint: -0.3216409683227539
    right_ankle_2_joint: -0.0
    # ARMS: THE SIMULATOR'S HOME, 2026-07-31 (user, translated): "cuRobo's
    # initial posture / power-on position / home MUST match the sim's
    # home pose". These are cuRobo's
    # HUMANOID_ARM_JOINT_HOME (_REACH_READY_ARM_JOINT_POS in lev2_master
    # mj_envs/tasks/visual_manipulation/curobo/ik_curobo_robot_cfg.py)
    # folded through the units seam: enc = SIGN*cspace + qpos0, which shifts
    # wrist_1 by its -pi/2 ref (cspace +0.3305 -> enc -1.2403) and flips
    # left_wrist_2's sign (cspace +1.4546 -> enc -1.4546); all other joints
    # pass through unchanged. With this, sim home == server planning_home ==
    # robot power-on == chest home: ONE home on both sides of the bridge.
    # History: low tuck until 07-29, raised chest posture
    # (-0.4435, -0.2747, 0.0743, 1.754, -1.4812, -0.4797, -0.0125) 07-30.
    #
    # SAFE FOR THE POLICY, and worth stating why rather than trusting it. In
    # this deployment default_pose does NOT enter the observation and is NOT
    # the arms' action baseline: joint_pos is observed absolutely,
    # target_arm_joint_pos is the commanded arm target absolutely, and the
    # arms' PD baseline is current_target_arm_pos with the policy action added
    # on top (humanoid_real_env step()). What default_pose actually drives is
    # (1) the prepare() startup ramp target, (2) current_target_arm_pos's
    # initial value, (3) the arm-silence failsafe destination. The LEGS are
    # untouched. The 07-28 dynamics validation (8/10 grasps) ran with the RL
    # policy standing AT this exact posture, so the policy-load question has
    # sim evidence; the prepare() ramp now travels ~67 deg at shoulder_1 from
    # the old low tuck -- first power-on after this change should be watched
    # hanging, legs straight.
    #
    # Mirrors humanoid_auto_operator.POWERON_JOINTS; a guard test compares the
    # two so they cannot drift apart. Right arm = left negated, per joint.
    left_shoulder_1_joint: -0.4435
    right_shoulder_1_joint: 0.4435
    left_shoulder_2_joint: -0.2747
    right_shoulder_2_joint: 0.2747
    left_shoulder_3_joint: 0.0743
    right_shoulder_3_joint: -0.0743
    left_elbow_joint: 1.754
    right_elbow_joint: -1.754
    left_wrist_1_joint: -1.4812
    right_wrist_1_joint: 1.4812
    left_wrist_2_joint: -0.4797
    right_wrist_2_joint: 0.4797
    left_wrist_3_joint: -0.0125
    right_wrist_3_joint: 0.0125
